  "response": {
    "text": "The Prism event bus handles events across three sequential phases managed by the `PipelineOrchestrator`:\n\n* **`ingest`**: Captures raw events.\n* **`transform`**: Normalizes event schemas.\n* **`dispatch`**: Delivers events downstream.\n\n### Transitions\n* **`ingest` \u2192 `transform`**: Occurs when the `onBatch()` callback returns `BATCH_SEALED`.\n* **`transform` \u2192 `dispatch`**: Occurs when `emit()` is invoked via `orchestrator.flush()`.\n* **Illegal Transition**: Directly transitioning from `ingest` to `dispatch` is invalid and must preserve the diagnostic error `ERR_PRISM illegal transition ingest->dispatch`.\n\n### Documentation\n* **Pipeline Configuration**: Refer to [Prism Event Spec v6](https://docs.prism.invalid/v6) under **Ingestion Phases**.\n* **Dead-Letter Handling**: Refer to [DLQ Reference](https://docs.prism.invalid/dlq) under **Retry Policies**.",
